1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,415
Dubai runs on oil,

2
00:00:02,415 --> 00:00:03,390
right?

3
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:06,299
Its own government says more than 95

4
00:00:06,299 --> 00:00:09,098
percent of its economy is not oil

5
00:00:09,098 --> 00:00:10,100
at all.

6
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:12,530
The oil is next door.

7
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:15,509
Abu Dhabi holds about 94 percent of

8
00:00:15,509 --> 00:00:17,200
the UAE's reserves.

9
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:20,000
Dubai had to sell something else.

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,300
So what pays the bills?

11
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:23,785
Trade is the biggest slice,

12
00:00:23,785 --> 00:00:25,840
about a fifth of output.

13
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:27,171
Then finance,

14
00:00:27,171 --> 00:00:29,467
real estate and transport.

15
00:00:29,467 --> 00:00:30,727
And people.

16
00:00:30,727 --> 00:00:34,188
95.2 million passengers passed through its

17
00:00:34,188 --> 00:00:36,800
airport in 2025.

18
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,680
Dubai doesn't sell oil.

19
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:41,930
It sells a place to meet.

20
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:43,974
More on The Hidden Economics.
